{"title":"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2018 AMC 10A #7</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">2018 AMC 12A #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Observations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Observations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many (not necessarily positive) integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/2/7728ccd643a9ca4505b5fa61fdcc32eec45aa172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4000\\cdot \\left(\\tfrac{2}{5}\\right)^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"84\" height=\"22\" /> an integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f186ed67e815eba219f18765a25e974c831706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }3 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }4 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }6 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }8 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }9 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Algebra)\">Solution 1 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da18869f564298c403c1de14e39521bd6a19ab29.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4000\\cdot \\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^n=\\left(2^5\\cdot5^3\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\cdot5^{-1}\\right)^n=2^{5+n}\\cdot5^{3-n}.\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"43\" />\nSince this expression is an integer, we need: \n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af42d23c82557954f79eb41c912161087ddeab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+n\\geq0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff9489402bbac84c65a44d8da468c4bba4e95712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq-5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97ff8f99b14f9a5e9b2dab1470e48013e1a2d0ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-n\\geq0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c99bc7e0d9a6fca6c4e2b0151ded0a79f2151c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\leq3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p></ol>\n<p>Taking the intersection gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2ee62592909bd9e900d69e4bb69cac5068cc37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5\\leq n\\leq3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> So, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f3818fc1a1302e30d6fb36aa395ef64698432cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-(-5)+1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"180\" height=\"30\" /> integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Observations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Observations)\">Solution 2 (Observations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Observations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/670780664b076280ac22cecd0e680befd9449c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4000\\cdot \\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" /> will be an integer if the denominator is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0929ed034079c23455c385741744274c1f69b61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. We also know that the denominator will always be a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for positive values and a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for all negative values. So we can proceed to divide \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0929ed034079c23455c385741744274c1f69b61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for each increasing positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> until we get a non-factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0929ed034079c23455c385741744274c1f69b61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> and also divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0929ed034079c23455c385741744274c1f69b61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f2a422001c5e957f7df528eaf618e0220ebb16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" /> for each decreasing negative value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. For positive values we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a56e4a5983419de5c8a8e683d4a81bba6396afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n= 1, 2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> and for negative values we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/8179864eebc8cd411eebf57f38c844c9880cb8ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n= -1, -2, -3, -4, -5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"17\" />. Also keep in mind that the expression will be an integer for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02349576cee613512cdf301a365f06c0760acab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, which gives us a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e96880a2ee1951870033a1cdbeb0ad262f7ac19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 3 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4958997854e6f09504e811deec533556e8344e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"204\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93032f1ab8b685d84a767a2fde0d9006a464b5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>The corresponding values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/670780664b076280ac22cecd0e680befd9449c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4000\\cdot \\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e12f4ad70889bb2ee4c2e8e92208c34fa1e45b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$390625, 156250, 62500, 25000, 10000, 4000, 1600, 640,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"409\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972ad1bf6cf4ae9dcefdf2be3bcc1f74c99ba676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$256,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>In total, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e96880a2ee1951870033a1cdbeb0ad262f7ac19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p>~Little ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vzyRAnpnJes\">https://youtu.be/vzyRAnpnJes</a>\n</p><p>Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZiZVIMmo260\">https://youtu.be/ZiZVIMmo260</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2vz_CnxsGMA\">https://youtu.be/2vz_CnxsGMA</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZhAZ1oPe5Ds?t=1763\">https://youtu.be/ZhAZ1oPe5Ds?t=1763</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A\">2018 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=